  "output": {
    "answer": "It rendered the actual built screens, not a description of them — every persona was pointed at the same real, working build on the device stated in their brief, not a mockup or a plan. But it was still synthetic in one key way: it ran against a fixed viewport, without real device chrome or the task-switching a real session has. That's what bit me — the panel called it DONE at 21:50, then my own iPhone the next morning showed a mostly unusable app. So it interacted with live UI, just not on live hardware.",
